                  High-order Remap Miniapp


Version 2.0, released on Nov 13, 2026
======================================

- Added runtime device selection through MFEM's `-d` option and GPU support for
  the main high-order, low-order and FCT solvers on CUDA and HIP devices.

- Added device kernels for partial-assembly residual-distribution and subcell
  residual-distribution methods in 2D and 3D, including optimized Q2 and Q3
  kernels.

- Made overlap- and matrix-sparsity-based bounds computations, shared-DOF
  reductions, mesh motion and the Taylor-Green velocity function
  device-friendly.

- Added synchronized product-field remapping, including high- and low-order
  product updates, ClipScale limiting and element-based FCT projection.

- Added the mass-based element-average low-order solver and an option to form
  solution bounds from the operator matrix sparsity pattern.

- Added bounds-preserving Forward Euler and Runge-Kutta time integration,
  including RK2, RK3, RK4 and RK6 schemes, and support for repeated time levels.

- Added automatic time-step selection and adjustment based on low-order bounds,
  with improved bounds verification and optional inactive-DOF masks.

- Added automatic generation of well-partitioned Cartesian meshes based on the
  dimension, MPI task count and requested number of elements per task.

- Added optional Caliper profiling and Adiak metadata, figures of merit for the
  main solver phases, and device-memory pool usage and high-water-mark
  reporting.

- Added a shared Umpire device-memory pool for MFEM and hypre, a configurable
  initial pool size, pool warm-up and optional GPU-aware MPI communication.

- Added CMake support with C++17, packaged dependency discovery, HIP builds,
  separate library and executable targets, installation rules and CTest tests.

- Added GitHub Actions regression testing, expanded CPU and GPU test coverage,
  and refreshed the reference results for new algorithms and MFEM interfaces.

- Added support for finite element orders zero and one, updated compatibility
  with newer MFEM APIs, and fixed CUDA, HIP and NVCC build issues.

- Fixed host-device synchronization and alias-memory transfers, product-remap
  and time-step errors, mass reporting, final remap mesh position, bounds
  checks, one-dimensional tests and several memory and round-off issues.


Version 1.0, released on Mar 30, 2020
=====================================

- Initial release.
